# DE10-Standard user-I/O pin reference
#
# Board:  Terasic DE10-Standard
# Device: 5CSXFC6D6F31C6 (Cyclone V SoC)
# I/O standard for every pin below: 3.3-V LVTTL
#
# PROVENANCE
# ----------
# Transcribed from Terasic's DE10_Standard golden-top pin assignments and
# cross-checked against two independent published .qsf files plus the
# DE10-Standard User Manual pin tables. All sources agree on every pin here.
#
#   https://github.com/umamibeef/vga-controller/blob/master/DE10_Standard_default.qsf
#   https://github.com/LeThanhHai-1610/DE10-Standard_miniproject/blob/master/Miniproject.qsf
#   https://ftp.intel.com/Public/Pub/fpgaup/pub/Intel_Material/Boards/DE10-Standard/DE10_Standard_User_Manual.pdf
#
# scripts/check_pins.py diffs syn/quartus/build_de10.tcl against this file,
# so a typo in a pin assignment is a build failure rather than a board that
# quietly does nothing. HEX0-HEX5 are listed for completeness; the current
# design does not drive them.
#
# format: <signal> <pin>
CLOCK_50 PIN_AF14
HEX0[0] PIN_W17
HEX0[1] PIN_V18
HEX0[2] PIN_AG17
HEX0[3] PIN_AG16
HEX0[4] PIN_AH17
HEX0[5] PIN_AG18
HEX0[6] PIN_AH18
HEX1[0] PIN_AF16
HEX1[1] PIN_V16
HEX1[2] PIN_AE16
HEX1[3] PIN_AD17
HEX1[4] PIN_AE18
HEX1[5] PIN_AE17
HEX1[6] PIN_V17
HEX2[0] PIN_AA21
HEX2[1] PIN_AB17
HEX2[2] PIN_AA18
HEX2[3] PIN_Y17
HEX2[4] PIN_Y18
HEX2[5] PIN_AF18
HEX2[6] PIN_W16
HEX3[0] PIN_Y19
HEX3[1] PIN_W19
HEX3[2] PIN_AD19
HEX3[3] PIN_AA20
HEX3[4] PIN_AC20
HEX3[5] PIN_AA19
HEX3[6] PIN_AD20
HEX4[0] PIN_AD21
HEX4[1] PIN_AG22
HEX4[2] PIN_AE22
HEX4[3] PIN_AE23
HEX4[4] PIN_AG23
HEX4[5] PIN_AF23
HEX4[6] PIN_AH22
HEX5[0] PIN_AF21
HEX5[1] PIN_AG21
HEX5[2] PIN_AF20
HEX5[3] PIN_AG20
HEX5[4] PIN_AE19
HEX5[5] PIN_AF19
HEX5[6] PIN_AB21
KEY[0] PIN_AJ4
KEY[1] PIN_AK4
